Package: DroneBioR
Title: Reproducible Drone Biomass Workflows for Multispectral Imagery
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Hugo Machado",
           family = "Rodrigues",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "rodrigues.machado.hugo@gmail.com")
Description: A reproducible R workflow for drone-based biomass research using
    multispectral imagery from MicaSense cameras such as the RedEdge series.
    'DroneBioR' wraps external photogrammetry engines (OpenDroneMap,
    'WebODM', 'Pix4Dmapper', 'Agisoft Metashape') to produce orthomosaics,
    digital surface and terrain models, dense point clouds and meshes, and
    then provides the scientific layer in R: alpha and no-data masking,
    radiometric scaling to reflectance, vegetation indices (NDVI, NDRE, EVI,
    SAVI, NDWI, GNDVI, CIrededge, MSAVI2 and VARI), canopy height models,
    point-cloud region-of-interest analysis, individual tree candidate
    detection, field sample extraction, baseline biomass models and a Shiny
    application for interactive exploration. The package targets academic
    and research use.
